  "assumptions_and_limits": [
    "Observed R1 is only eight Flash requests, with one protocol format failure; it is cost evidence, not a valid R2 calibration or a statistical guarantee about Pro.",
    "Doubling or quadrupling observed growth is a stated stress assumption, not a worst-case model-output or game-observation bound.",
    "The output-cap sensitivity fixes output at 2048 while retaining 2x observed prompt/message growth. It isolates cost sensitivity and is intentionally not a self-consistent maximum-growth trajectory.",
    "No truncation, history compaction, step reduction, or prompt-semantic change is proposed by this artifact.",
    "Theoretical envelopes apply the request-byte limit at every call plus 1024 tokens per message and max output. They are rigorous transport-accounting upper envelopes under the fixed 2*i message loop, not claimed attainable tokenizer/environment maxima.",
    "A true attainable worst trajectory cannot be determined from R1: token-to-UTF8 expansion and tool-observation size lack a per-round bound. Token cap 2048 is not a guarantee of a 1-2 KB message increment.",
    "A separate saturation scenario of 2048 fresh retained output tokens each round creates 2048*N*(N-1)/2 repeated prompt tokens before observations, assuming additive retained token accounting; for 64 calls these alone plus outputs cost Pro 47.75215104 CNY without cache. This is a sensitivity construction, not a formal tokenizer bound.",
    "The proposed 24 child caps sum to 220 CNY, greater than the shared pilot cap. The coordinator may proceed by settling actual costs and reserving each next balanced block, but cannot guarantee all rows if actual costs approach child caps.",
    "The shared 200 CNY pilot and 2000 CNY overall limits remain unchanged; every real dispatched call still needs its conservative reservation and uncertainty must stop or remain reserved.",
    "Peak price estimates are planning/accounting values, not provider invoices; cached savings are excluded from projections."
  ]
